ange  lateral yellow  anterior blue  posterior black   serially  sectioned from medial to lateral  The cut surface is tan yellow and  homogeneous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue  which constitutes  approximately 70  of the breast parenchyma  No discrete lesions are grossly  identified  The specimen is submitted in its entirety   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  2 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sequential cross sections  medial to lateral  2 frags each  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  2 frags  ESS   Blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include possible mass is noted per specimen radiograph  The  specimen radiograph is interpreted via Centricity and demonstrates the area of  interest marked by radiology   SEK mmm  CASE NUMBER   REMOVED_CASE_ID   By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Jane E  Brock M B   B S   Ph D   Electronically signed on  Friday REMOVED_MONTH 27   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 09 21 12PM  ADDENDUM   Deeper histological levels on the intraductal papilloma present   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   show the  atypical E cadherin negative cells noted within the papilloma develop an  apocrine appearance and have higher nuclear grade than typically seen in  classic ALH  These cells are  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  keratin positive and ER and PR negative   ER and PR negativity is commonly seen in apocrine lesions  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  negative  0   The atypical cells are confined to the papilloma and their  significance is unclear  Overall the diagnosis is best considered atypical  hyperplasia with apocrine features confined to a papilloma  Dr  Susan Lester  and Dr  Andrea Richardson both reviewed these additional slides and concur with  the diagnosis   Addendum  1 by Jane E  Brock M B   B S   Ph D   Electronically signed on  Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 03   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 03 05PM   report_end  , no_FlatEpithelial.
