tic change  with cystic spaces measuring up to  0 4cm in maximum dimension  All of the grossly abnormal tissue is submitted   There are no areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma  The remainder of  the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  All margins are taken perpendicular   Approximately 40  of the specimen is submitted for histologic examination   Micro  1   lateral margin  RSS   Micro  2   medial margin  RSS   Micro  3   superior margin  RSS   Micro  4   inferior margin  RSS   Micro  5 6   posterior margin  RSS   Micro  7   anterior margin  RSS   Micro  8 10  additional anteroinferior margin  RSS   Reports to  KAELIN  CAROLYN  MARY M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS   report_end  , no_FlatEpithelial.
